{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_dElJ2XUNhYCjJtxVvaIRvIMx","content":"1050\t(defn- outcome-node\n1051\t  [tag value]\n1052\t  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n1053\t\n1054\t\n1055\t(defn- call-entry\n1056\t  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\"\n1057\t  []\n1058\t  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n1059\t        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n1060\t        outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"entry_outcome\"))\n1061\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1062\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1063\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1064\t        binding-error (outcome-node\n1065\t                        error-tag\n1066\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1067\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n1068\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n1069\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n1070\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1071\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n1072\t        entry-body (u/let1\n1073\t                     outcome\n1074\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1075\t                                (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1076\t                                binding-error)\n1077\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1078\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 0))\n1079\t                                       (u/lit ok-tag))\n1080\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))\n1081\t                                (u/app raise\n1082\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\n1083\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\n1084\t                                                     (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\n1085\t        ;; The private lane forwards the body's outcome in tail position.\n1086\t        ;; The public entry still converts outcomes to value/raise normally.\n1087\t        ;; The compiler's token packet - a two-element vector whose first\n1088\t        ;; element is the compiler-held token - selects the private tail\n1089\t        ;; lane on the SAME unary entry: no record unwrap, no map lookups.\n1090\t        ;; A guest cannot forge it: the token is compiler-held and the\n1091\t        ;; reserved-prefix regime refuses binding or shadowing it. Maps\n1092\t        ;; keep the ordinary record path. The vector guard is required:\n1093\t        ;; data/nth refuses non-vectors, and dsg__get reads vectors as\n1094\t        ;; nil whenever the program defines its own get.\n1095\t        packet (u/if-node\n1096\t                 (u/app (u/v 'data/vector?) (u/v invocation))\n1097\t                 (u/if-node\n1098\t                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1099\t                          (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v invocation) (u/lit 0))\n1100\t                          (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1101\t                   (u/app (u/v body) (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v invocation) (u/lit 1)))\n1102\t                   ;; a vector without the compiler-held token is NOT the\n1103\t                   ;; record path: applying the body here would hand every\n1104\t                   ;; forged vector the private lane. Refuse explicitly.\n1105\t                   (u/lit [:yin.k/error\n1106\t                           {:yin.k/message \"Invocation is neither an authenticated packet nor an invocation record\"\n1107\t                            :yin.k/data {}}]))\n1108\t                 (u/if-node\n1109\t                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1110\t                          (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\n1111\t                                 (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\n1112\t                          (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1113\t                   (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1114\t                              (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1115\t                              binding-error)\n1116\t                   entry-body))\n1117\t        entry (u/lam [invocation] packet)]\n1118\t    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1119\t\n1120\t\n1121\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n1122\t  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n1123\t   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1124\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n1125\t  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n1126\t        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n1127\t                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n1128\t        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n1129\t        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n1130\t        ;; it never applies a source-supplied predicate. An equal immutable\n1131\t        ;; reconstruction is the same value, not admission of different data.\n1132\t        witness (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_admission) (u/v descriptor-name))\n1133\t        published (u/let1 descriptor-name canonical\n1134\t                          (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v descriptor-name)"}
