commit 358e2f1b2b3c33b795890ab1977115df3be9cb8d
Author:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Nov 3 06:08:33 2026 +0700
Commit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 06:08:33 2026 +0700

    fix(yang.clojure): D2 revise — forged vectors refuse, authenticity and assoc branches restored, exact counts recorded
    
    The quality gate's four items, addressed: (1) the packet dispatch's
    alternate branch no longer applies the private body to a forged vector -
    it returns an explicit refusal outcome, so [42], [nil [42]], [], and
    overlong vectors never reach the body; (2) adversarial regressions on
    both evaluators: five forged shapes against a side-effecting marker body,
    each asserted not to run it; (3) the dsg__witness callable? guard
    restored (dropped in transit); (4) the native-assoc implementation of
    dsg__assoc restored verbatim for programs that don't shadow assoc.
    Exact instruction counts at the unchanged 2M budget: check-accepted
    walker/semantic well under budget; check-assume-have-discharge walker
    1,837,052 / semantic 1,002,469 - both complete inside 2M with headroom.
    Focused gate: counts {pass 102, recorded-upstream-failure 2,
    recorded-deviation 2, blocked 0}, exactly the by-design assertion
    failing; forgery regressions 5/5 green; kondo 0/0.

