{"role":"assistant","content":"## Verdict: **REJECT — the implementation is repaired, but its adversarial regression is vacuous**\n\n### P1: the test refuses before reaching packet dispatch\n\n`test-common-call-token-packet-forgery-refuses` calls the extracted raw entry through ordinary source lowering (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1356-1364`). Dynamic admission rejects that raw closure before the entry executes.\n\nI ran the five forms and every one returned:\n\n```clojure\n[:yin.k/error\n {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\n  :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee {:type :closure}}}]\n```\n\nTherefore these tests would also pass against the rejected implementation whose forged-vector alternate applied the body.\n\nTwo further test defects:\n\n- `run-outcome` uses only `tu/create-vm`, i.e. the walker (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1137-1145`); it does not test both evaluators.\n- `(not= :private-body-entered payload)` is too weak: a successful body invocation would ordinarily be wrapped as `[:yin.k/ok :private-body-entered]`, which also satisfies the assertion.\n\nConstruct a **direct UAST application** of the extracted entry, run that same AST through both `walker-run` and `semantic-run`, and assert:\n\n- an error outcome, not success;\n- the body’s observable marker never occurs;\n- ideally the exact refusal for nonempty forged vectors.\n\nUsing `probe/note` in the body and checking `effect-log` would prove non-entry directly. The existing intra-unit tests already exercise the authenticated positive path.\n\n### Confirmed repaired\n\n- The production forged-vector alternate now returns an error and no longer applies `body` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1095-1116`).\n- The `dsg__witness` callable guard is restored.\n- Both `dsg__assoc` implementations are restored.\n- The discharge counts—walker **1,837,052**, semantic **1,002,469**—are within 2M.\n\n### Still outstanding\n\nThe ruling requested exact counts for **both** formerly blocked fixtures. `check-accepted` is still reported only as “well under”; supply its walker and semantic counts.\n\nLanding remains blocked on a real both-evaluator packet-dispatch regression and those two counts. The production authenticity fix itself looks correct."}
